#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""brood — natal literals are domain-tagged, so 0.4-threshold ≠ 0.4-opacity.

Query a commit or a diff (never FILE:LINE). Every birth cohort that change
touches is scored at HEAD. Keys still inflect: t1 ↔ driftDelay from the same
line's history, present_threshold ↔ presentThreshold by snake/camel.

The flip from erst: a natal literal is not a global token. The binder at
birth (threshold = 0.4) is the domain tag. A leftover 0.4 bound to alpha /
opacity / rgba is a different cohort, even if the bytes match and even if
both were born in the same commit.

This is not aka (no inflection catalog). This is not also (no FILE:LINE).
This is not leftover-name search. The change is the query.
"""

